<title>USA: EA Industries names new president/CEO.</title>
<headline>EA Industries names new president/CEO.</headline>
<dateline>WEST LONG BRANCH, N.J. 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>EA Industries Inc said it named former Unisys Corp executive Frank Brandenberg as its president and chief executive officer.</p>
<p>Brandenberg was formerly group vice president and general manager of personal computers and NT servers at Unisys. As president he succeeds Joseph Spalliero, who resigned in December as president. The position of chief executive was formerly held by company chairman Irwin Gross, who remains chairman.</p>
<p>At EA Industries, Brandenberg will focus on the company's core business of electronic contract manufacturing. In a statement, he said his first priority will be to return EA to profitability.</p>
</text>
